Figure 1 presents a box plot illustrating the comparative adjuvanticity of Nano-11 and aluminum hydroxide (AH) with recombinant protective antigen (rPA). The plot shows anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with rPA alone or adjuvanted with different doses (200, 50, and 12.5 µg) of Nano-11 or AH. While both adjuvants significantly enhance antibody titers compared to rPA alone, Nano-11 demonstrates comparable or superior immunopotentiation. Notably, Nano-11 maintains high IgG titers even at a low dose of 12.5 µg, a concentration at which AH shows significantly reduced efficacy, suggesting Nano-11's effectiveness at lower doses.